# Day 57

**33km / 7.5 hours**

*Koitiata to Bulls*

The day began dry enough so I packed up while that was still the case and set off. It was back on the beach for three hours or fifteen km or so. Fun stuff. Then it was some road that made me miss the beach. 

![A bird flying over the water](./beach-bird.avif)

The only interesting part of the road walk was the RNZAF (Royal New Zealand Air Force) flying a bunch of military planes and even a helicopter all over the place. I guess they were doing test runs for training/exercises. 

![A plane flying over for fun](./plane.avif)

Finally got into Bulls, a charming town on an intersection of a major road with a single gimmick/joke that they really lean into. Basically it's using words that end in -ble and replacing it with -bull. e.g. the police station has const-a-bull on it.